  "body_html": "<h1>Epsilon-Optimal Strategy</h1>\n<p>Given $\\varepsilon&gt;0$, a row strategy $x \\in \\Delta(I)$ is <strong>maxmin\n$\\varepsilon$-optimal</strong> if its guarantee meets at least\n$\\operatorname{val}(A) - \\varepsilon$:\n$$\n  \\min_{j \\in J} E_A(x, j) \\ge \\operatorname{val}(A) - \\varepsilon.\n$$\nA $0$-optimal strategy is an optimal strategy. The dual definition (a column\nstrategy $y$ is $\\varepsilon$-optimal when\n$\\max_{i \\in I} E_A(i, y) \\le \\operatorname{val}(A) + \\varepsilon$) applies to\nplayer 2.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Def. 2.2.6] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MathFoundationsGameTheory.pdf</code>. Epsilon-optimal and optimal strategies.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
